# Cursor Project Rules

## Requirement Discipline

- Never invent requirements, features, files, fields, abstractions, or refactors that the user did not explicitly ask for.
- If any requirement is ambiguous, ask a clarifying question before making code changes.
- Before implementation, restate the requested scope in 3-6 bullet points and follow only that scope.

## Strict Execution

- Follow every user requirement exactly.
- Do not rename public APIs, files, classes, or functions unless requested.
- Do not make "helpful" extra improvements outside the requested scope.

## Architecture

- Separate data models and business logic into different modules.
- Avoid mixing DTOs/entities with calculation or workflow logic in the same module unless explicitly requested.

## Package Management

- Use `requirements.txt` for all pip installations. Never use `pip install -e .` or `pyproject.toml` for dependency management in this project.

## Change Safety

- Prefer minimal diffs.
- Preserve existing behavior unless the user asked to change it.
- When editing existing code, explain what changed and what was intentionally left unchanged.
